# Minimal build-context exclusion list. openab/Dockerfile.radar-agent's
# build context is the repo root (docker-compose.yml's `context: .`) --
# without this file, `docker build`/`docker compose build` sends the
# entire working tree (including git history, any local .env, gitignored
# openab/.local/ secrets, and every developer's __pycache__/venv) to the
# Docker daemon, even though the Dockerfile's own COPY instructions are
# selective about what actually lands in an image layer. Reproducible,
# secret-free build context, not merely a reproducible image.

.git/
.gitignore

# Never send real secrets, even though nothing in the Dockerfile ever
# COPYs these paths -- the point is these bytes should never even leave
# the host into the build context/daemon.
.env
openab/.local/

# Caches/bytecode/venvs -- never needed in the build context, and their
# contents can vary per developer machine/run, which is exactly what
# "reproducible build context" means to exclude.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local SQLite databases and other scratch artifacts developers may have
# sitting in the working tree.
*.db

# Editor/OS cruft.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
